    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d799">

                <pb facs="d798-4" n="4" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/d798-4"/>

                <head>799. Letter from Freers to Johnson<anchor n="1" xml:id="d799-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1957-03-21">March 21, 1957</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear Alex:</salute>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d799-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d799-1"/>
                <p>Walter McConaughy has just informed me
                    that your tentative plans for home leave call for leaving directly for the
                    States from Geneva about May 10.</p>
                <pb facs="1402" n="1355" type="typeset" xml:id="pg1355"/>
                <p>I regret to have to bring up a complication but thought you should know that a
                    meeting of the Eastern European Chiefs of Mission is now scheduled for May 10
                    through 13 in Vienna. Burke Elbrick will preside, and among others expecting to
                    attend are Messrs. Henderson, Murphy,
                    Perkins and Bill Clark from USIA. We feel it very important that you be there to
                    present your views about the situation in Czechoslovakia at the meeting.</p>
                <p>I hope the delay of a few days will not seriously disrupt your home leave plans.
                    You will be receiving more specific information about the meeting very
                    shortly.</p>
                <p>Best regards,</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Edward L.
                            Freers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
